# Banding with evasion (CR 702.22h and its example): a creature declared as a blocker of one member of a band blocks every
# member, even one it could not have been declared blocking. Bot1's Mesa Pegasus (1/1 flying, banding) attacks in a band with
# Guerrilla Gorilla. Bot2's Llanowar Elves can't block the Pegasus (flying, CR 702.9b) - refused - but blocks the Gorilla,
# and so the Pegasus is blocked too: nothing reaches Bot2. Bot1 divides the Elves' 1 (CR 702.22k) and puts it on the Gorilla,
# which lives; the band's 1 + 2 kill the Elves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mesa Pegasus
Guerrilla Gorilla
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mesa Pegasus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Mesa Pegasus > Bot2; Guerrilla Gorilla > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Guerrilla Gorilla)
! Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Mesa Pegasus)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Guerrilla Gorilla)
[T5 Bot1.Blockers]
? Combat.Blocks = Llanowar Elves > Guerrilla Gorilla; Llanowar Elves > Mesa Pegasus
Bot1.AssignDamage(Llanowar Elves > Guerrilla Gorilla: 1)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Damage = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mesa Pegasus.Damage = 0
